       canvas is ~72px narrower than the viewport (.wrap 40 + .lab-page 8 +
       .panel 24), so a 412px phone gets a 315x197 frame and the corner
       panels, the phase chip and the instrument cluster all land on top of
       each other. min-height lets the ratio relax toward portrait exactly
       when it needs to, with no breakpoint to keep in sync: above ~470px of
       canvas the ratio still wins. */
    min-height: 400px;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: linear-gradient(#b9c6cf, #e7e2d6);
  }

  /* ---- viewport overlay: HUD panels float on the canvas itself, same
